 - Writes require the `contributor` or `manager` role in the project. Users who can read but not write get 403.
 - Contributors may only modify tasks assigned to themselves, and may not reassign tasks. Managers may modify any task.
 - Only managers may delete tasks.
+- Moving a task (`/move`) needs the same edit right as modifying it in the
+  current project (so contributors move only their own tasks), and the
+  `contributor` or `manager` role in the target project (else 403). The target
+  must be readable by the user (else 404), not archived (else 409), and differ
+  from the current project (else 400). The task keeps its assignee, so the
+  assignee must already be a contributor or manager of the target (else 400).
 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
 
